{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "Research Harness — tool dispatch, memory validation and forged-call rejection (run B)",
  "description": "Parcours B of the spec #219 trial: a Project Tour assembled from a single measured Research-Harness run (runId 49a4cdfa, one `--code --knowledge` attempt at source revision `2f1ebcf`) that answered the frozen question and read one prepared Knowledge entry in-run. Anchors are unique code patterns verified in this checkout.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "description": "**Orientation.** `packages/exploration-poc` is a small research harness: a CLI takes one Research Question plus flags and budgets, an `explore` loop in `explore.ts` alternates model calls with dispatched tool calls (`list`, `search`, `read`, `git`, sandbox `code` runs, and in Knowledge mode `memory_list`/`memory_read`), until the model returns a final JSON report that must pass citation validation.\n\nThree protections shape this route: model input is masked before every call, every tool call goes through a single dispatch chain whose rejections are named, and Knowledge or Memory entries are validated deterministically before anything executes.\n\n**Diagram — Context view**\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  Operator[\"Operator with one research question\"] -->|\"asks one run\"| CLI[\"cli.ts entry point\"]\n  CLI -->|\"flags, budget, output lock\"| Loop[\"explore loop in explore.ts\"]\n  Loop -->|\"tool calls\"| Tools[\"Workspace tools: list, search, read, git\"]\n  Loop -->|\"codeMode branch\"| Sandbox[\"QuickJS sandbox: code, function_try, memory_run\"]\n  Loop -->|\"knowledge mode\"| Knowledge[\"memory_list, memory_read: verified library\"]\n  Loop -->|\"masked history every call\"| Model[\"mistral-small-latest model node\"]\n  Model -->|\"tool calls or final JSON\"| Loop\n```\n\nWork zones: the CLI, loop, masking, memory and knowledge seams all live in `packages/exploration-poc/src/` (`cli.ts`, `explore.ts`, `mask.ts`, `memory.ts`, `knowledge.ts`); this trial's own records — report, Knowledge copy, run outputs — sit under `poc/spec219-trial/`.\n\nFacts in this Tour come from a measured harness run (`runId 49a4cdfa`, `mistral-small-latest`, 11 model calls, 8 tool calls, status `complete`) produced against source revision `2f1ebcf`; anchors below are unique code patterns verified in this checkout."
    },
    {
      "title": "CLI entry point — flags, mode gate, model construction",
      "description": "`cli.ts` parses the workspace, `--output-file`, `--code`, budget flags and the mode flags, builds the Mistral model from the environment, acquires the output-file lock, then calls `explore()`.\n\nThe gate that matters here: `--memory` and `--knowledge` are mutually exclusive, and the CLI throws the shared `MEMORY_KNOWLEDGE_EXCLUSIVE_ERROR` **before any model call**. Run B launched with exactly `--code --knowledge`, so Memory Functions never existed in that process.",
      "file": "packages/exploration-poc/src/cli.ts",
      "pattern": "throw new Error\\(MEMORY_KNOWLEDGE_EXCLUSIVE_ERROR\\)"
    },
    {
      "title": "The explore model node — masked history in, tool calls out",
      "description": "Each loop iteration wraps the whole transcript in `complete(maskObservations(state.messages, config.context.keepToolResults, spilled), ...)` — the model never sees an unmasked history. The same call site passes `codeMode` and whether a knowledge library is attached, recomputes the output-token allowance from the remaining budget, and disables tools on the finalizing call.\n\nIn run B this loop ran 11 model calls (70,517 input / 4,446 output tokens) around 8 dispatched tool calls and ended with `status: complete`.",
      "file": "packages/exploration-poc/src/explore.ts",
      "pattern": "complete\\(maskObservations"
    },
    {
      "title": "Tool dispatch — every call name is matched exactly once",
      "description": "After each model reply, dispatch is a single `if` / `else if` chain: `readScratch` first, then the workspace tools, then the `codeMode` branch for `code`, `function_try` and `memory_run`, then the Knowledge branches `memory_list` (name and description only) and `memory_read` (deterministic verification, then the validated Markdown body). Any name outside the chain reaches the final `else throw new Error('Unknown tool or invalid arguments')`.\n\nRun B dispatched exactly 8 calls, all through this chain: one `list`, four `search` queries, `memory_list`, and one `memory_read` of the Knowledge entry — no forged call was ever produced.",
      "file": "packages/exploration-poc/src/explore.ts",
      "pattern": "else if \\(codeMode"
    },
    {
      "title": "Forged calls are named, not hidden",
      "description": "Three named rejections close the seams. A `memory_run` whose id never appeared among the model's attempts hits `throw new Error('Unknown script')` before anything executes; malformed arguments are refused with `Invalid parameters`; any call name outside the chain is refused with `Unknown tool or invalid arguments`.\n\nAll three surface to the model as ordinary observations, so nothing fails silently and nothing is retried automatically. Knowledge reads share the design: a failed verification returns exactly `invalid` — no body, no cited path, no hash value.",
      "file": "packages/exploration-poc/src/explore.ts",
      "pattern": "throw new Error\\('Unknown script'\\)"
    },
    {
      "title": "Memory validation before anything executes",
      "description": "Validation is deterministic and happens before content moves. In `memory.ts`, the zod `entrySchema` rejects malformed stored entries and `validateCanonicalName` enforces identifier-style names. In `knowledge.ts` (the #220 seam), every declared SHA-256 proof is re-hashed against the workspace bytes; a stale entry is refused with `file_hash_mismatch`.\n\nRun B exercised the live path: the entry `harness_dispatch_and_forgery` was discovered via `memory_list`, read via `memory_read` (verified in 5 ms), and the model then worked from that validated body — the pinned hashes here matched `2f1ebcf` exactly.",
      "file": "packages/exploration-poc/src/memory.ts",
      "pattern": "const entrySchema = z\\.object\\("
    },
    {
      "title": "Observation masking — old tool results shrink to stubs",
      "description": "Before every model call, `maskObservations` keeps the last `keep` tool results verbatim (`config.context.keepToolResults`, 8) and replaces older results above `MASK_MIN_BYTES` (2000) with a one-line stub `{ omitted: true, note, bytes, head }`, where `head` keeps the first 300 characters and `note` names the original call (and any scratch spill).\n\nThis is why 11 model calls stayed affordable, and why a reader must trust the final JSON over its masked history: the stub itself says to rely on the noted result, not on the masked-away bytes.",
      "file": "packages/exploration-poc/src/mask.ts",
      "pattern": "export const MASK_MIN_BYTES = 2000"
    }
  ]
}
